  "id": "Compound::DB08871 - Gene::81027",
  "verbalization": "Eribulin is implicated in the inhibition of microtubules, a mechanism shared with drugs like Ixabepilone and Docetaxel, both of which bind to Tubb1. The evidence suggests that Eribulin interacts with Tubb1 through a series of molecular pathways, with Ixabepilone acting as a bridge in both pathways. The lowest common ancestor of Eribulin and Ixabepilone points to the Tubulin Binding Agent, a class of molecules that are common in microtubule-targeting agents. This shared pathway implies a potential mechanism by which Eribulin may influence Tubb1, possibly through the same or related molecular interactions. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of Ixabepilone as a central mediator in the interaction between Eribulin and Tubb1, reinforcing the notion that Eribulin's effect on Tubb1 is mediated through a common biological target.",
